{"step_index":7506,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-24T16:06:54Z","thinking":"Initial assessment focuses on determining the number of cases to process. First, check if a batch size is provided and valid; if so, use that. Otherwise, inspect the input for explicit case identifiers. If identifiers are found, their count determines the case count; otherwise, assume a default of one case.\n\n\nTimeouts are being configured based on the determined case count, establishing start, first-token, stagnation, and hard-ceiling values. Logging confirms prompt submission with details on timeout tiers. A JavaScript function is prepared to check for ongoing generation activity by identifying stop buttons and active spinners within the interface.\n\n\nError conditions are being checked by examining alerts for specific failure messages; if found, the process is flagged as erroneous. Active generation is determined by detecting the presence of visual indicators like stop buttons or activity spinners. A count of model-generated turns is being established by analyzing the structure of conversation segments within the interface.\n\n\nA mechanism to differentiate between user and model turns is being established, considering various attributes within conversation segments. This involves inspecting role assignments, class names, author labels, and the presence of child elements to distinguish between user prompts and model responses. Turns are being iterated backward to identify consecutive model-generated content, focusing on the end of the conversation.\n\n\nModel turns are being extracted, filtering content chunks to remove UI elements, thoughts, and nested content to isolate the core generated text. Irrelevant elements are being temporarily hidden to prevent their inclusion in the extracted text. This process focuses extraction on the essential model responses.\n\n\nExtracted text is being assembled.  UI elements are temporarily hidden to prevent noise during text extraction, ensuring the focus remains on core model responses.  The state, turn indicators, and potential errors are checked.  The extracted content is checked against the timeout.\n\n\nJavaScript extraction errors are being handled, checking for browser closure or persistent failures.  If errors persist beyond a threshold, extraction is aborted.  A check for fatal errors within the environment is in place.  The system state variables are analyzed to determine the next step in the extraction process, focusing on whether a response has started.\n\n\nGeneration start is being tracked, moving to an active state upon detecting activity or text. A timeout is in place to handle scenarios where generation fails to initiate within a defined period, yielding an error if the timeout is exceeded.\n\nThe presence of the first token confirms the start of generation; this marks a key milestone for progress tracking.\n\n\nText generation progress is being tracked, looking for new tokens to confirm growth. A timeout is in place to catch instances where the model remains idle without producing content after prompt submission. Stable, non-growing text is being monitored against generation termination.\n\n\nGeneration stability is being evaluated by monitoring text length over time. If text remains unchanged for a predetermined duration, the generation is considered complete. Stagnation is also checked; if text fails to grow for a specified timeout, an error is reported.\n\nThe current state and extracted text are yielded continuously. The process will run until completion or if a hard ceiling is reached. If the hard ceiling is reached before the generation completes, an error is logged.\n\n\nGeneration terminated due to exceeding the hard timeout limit. Detailed timing metrics are being logged to assess the generation's progress and identify potential bottlenecks.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Implement 3-state machine, adaptive timeouts, and timing logs in send_prompt_and_stream","EndLine":716,"Instruction":"Replace polling loop in send_prompt_and_stream with 3-state machine, adaptive timeouts, and milestone timing logs","ReplacementContent":"        # Determine case count from batch_size or prompt inspection\n        case_count = batch_size if (batch_size is not None and batch_size > 0) else None\n        if not case_count:\n            cid_count = prompt.count('\"case_id\"') or prompt.count(\"'case_id'\")\n            case_count = cid_count if cid_count > 0 else 1\n\n        t_cfg = self.get_adaptive_timeouts(case_count)\n\n        # Lifecycle State Tracking\n        current_state = self.STATE_NO_RESPONSE_STARTED\n        t_submit = time.time()\n        t_turn_detected: Optional[float] = None\n        t_first_token: Optional[float] = None\n        t_last_growth = t_submit\n        stability_start_time: Optional[float] = None\n        prev_text = \"\"\n        consecutive_js_errors = 0\n\n        logger.info(\n            f\"[{case_count} cases] Prompt submitted ({len(prompt)} chars). \"\n            f\"Timeout Tier: {t_cfg['tier']} | Start: {t_cfg['initial_start_timeout']:.0f}s | \"\n            f\"First Token: {t_cfg['first_token_timeout']:.0f}s | Stagnation: {t_cfg['stagnation_timeout']:.0f}s | \"\n            f\"Ceiling: {t_cfg['hard_ceiling']:.0f}s\"\n        )\n\n        js_fetch_state = '''(initialCount) => {\n            // 1. Generation Running Check (Stop button or active spinners)\n            const stopBtn = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('button')).find(b => {\n                const a = (b.getAttribute('aria-label') || '').toLowerCase();\n                const t = (b.innerText || b.textContent || '').trim().toLowerCase();\n                return (a === 'stop' || a.includes('stop run') || a.includes('stop generat') || a === 'cancel run' ||\n                        t === 'stop' || t.includes('stop run') || t.includes('stop generat') || t === 'cancel run') && !b.disabled;\n            });\n            // Also check if there is an active spinner indicating thinking\n            const hasSpinner = document.querySelector('mat-progress-spinner, .typing-indicator, ms-spinner, .thought-activity-host[aria-expanded=\"true\"]') !== null;\n            const isRunning = Boolean(stopBtn) || hasSpinner;\n\n            // Check for internal errors\n            let hasError = false;\n            const alertEl = document.querySelector('mat-snack-bar-container, .toast, [role=\"alert\"]');\n            if (alertEl) {\n                const atxt = (alertEl.innerText || alertEl.textContent || '').toLowerCase();\n                if (atxt.includes('permission denied') || atxt.includes('internal error') || atxt.includes('failed to generate')) {\n                    hasError = true;\n                }\n            }\n\n            if (hasError) {\n                return { text: \"\", is_running: isRunning, is_done: false, has_error: true, new_turn_started: true, model_count: 0 };\n            }\n\n            // Find all chat turns\n            const allTurns = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('ms-chat-turn, .chat-turn-container, .chat-turn, [data-turn-role]'));\n            if (allTurns.length === 0) {\n                return { text: \"\", is_running: isRunning, is_done: false, has_error: false, new_turn_started: isRunning, model_count: 0 };\n            }\n\n            // Count model turns\n            const modelTurns = allTurns.filter(t => {\n                const role = (t.getAttribute('data-turn-role') || '').toLowerCase();\n                const cls = (t.getAttribute('class') || '').toLowerCase();\n                const author = (t.querySelector('.author-label, .turn-author, .role-label')?.innerText || '').toLowerCase();\n                const hasUserChild = t.querySelector('[data-turn-role=\"User\"], .user-prompt-container, .user') !== null;\n                const isUser = role === 'user' || cls.includes('user') || author.includes('user') || hasUserChild;\n                if (isUser) return false;\n                return role === 'model' || cls.includes('model') || author.includes('model') || Boolean(t.querySelector('ms-thought-chunk, .thought-activity-host, ms-prompt-chunk, .model-prompt-container'));\n            });\n\n            const currentModelCount = modelTurns.length;\n            const newTurnStarted = (currentModelCount > initialCount) || isRunning;\n\n            // Iterate backwards to find all consecutive model turns at the end of the chat\n            const modelTurnsToExtract = [];\n            for (let i = allTurns.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {\n                const t = allTurns[i];\n                const role = (t.getAttribute('data-turn-role') || '').toLowerCase();\n                const cls = (t.getAttribute('class') || '').toLowerCase();\n                const author = (t.querySelector('.author-label, .turn-author, .role-label')?.innerText || '').toLowerCase();\n                const hasUserChild = t.querySelector('[data-turn-role=\"User\"], .user-prompt-container, .user') !== null;\n                const isUser = role === 'user' || cls.includes('user') || author.includes('user') || hasUserChild;\n                \n                if (isUser) {\n                    break;\n                }\n                modelTurnsToExtract.push(t);\n            }\n\n            // They were collected backwards, so reverse them to chronological order\n            modelTurnsToExtract.reverse();\n\n            // Extract text from these model turns\n            let fullText = \"\";\n            let isDone = !isRunning;\n\n            modelTurnsToExtract.forEach(currentNode => {\n                // Extract text from specific content chunks to avoid UI garbage and thoughts\n                const chunks = Array.from(currentNode.querySelectorAll('ms-text-chunk, ms-code-block, ms-code-chunk, .cmark-node'));\n                if (chunks.length > 0) {\n                    // Filter out nested chunks to prevent duplicates (e.g. cmark-node inside ms-text-chunk)\n                    const topLevelChunks = chunks.filter(c => {\n                        return !c.parentElement.closest('ms-text-chunk, ms-code-block, ms-code-chunk, .cmark-node');\n                    });\n\n                    topLevelChunks.forEach(chunk => {\n                        // Skip thoughts entirely\n                        if (chunk.closest('ms-thought-chunk, .thought-activity-host')) return;\n                        \n                        const selectorsToRemove = '.mat-expansion-panel-header, .code-block-header, button, mat-icon, .material-symbols-outlined, ms-citation-chunk, .citation';\n                        \n                        // Temporarily hide elements we don't want to extract\n                        const hiddenStates = [];\n                        chunk.querySelectorAll(selectorsToRemove).forEach(n => {\n                            hiddenStates.push({ node: n, display: n.style.display });\n                            n.style.display = 'none';\n                        });\n                        \n                        try {\n                            const t = (chunk.innerText || '').trim();\n                            if (t) {\n                                if (fullText.length > 0) fullText += '\\\\n\\\\n';\n                                fullText += t;\n                            }\n                        } finally {\n                            // Restore visibility\n                            hiddenStates.forEach(item => {\n                                item.node.style.display = item.display;\n                            });\n                        }\n                    });\n                }\n            });\n\n            return {\n                text: fullText.trim(),\n                is_running: isRunning,\n                is_done: isDone,\n                has_error: false,\n                new_turn_started: newTurnStarted,\n                model_count: currentModelCount\n            };\n        }'''\n\n        while (time.time() - t_submit) < t_cfg[\"hard_ceiling\"]:\n            now = time.time()\n            elapsed = now - t_submit\n\n            if not self.page or self.page.is_closed() or self.is_shutting_down:\n                logger.info(\"Browser session closed or shutting down. Exiting stream.\")\n                break\n\n            try:\n                state = await self.page.evaluate(js_fetch_state, initial_model_count)\n                consecutive_js_errors = 0\n            except Exception as e:\n                err_msg = str(e).lower()\n                if \"closed\" in err_msg or \"destroyed\" in err_msg or \"target\" in err_msg or self.is_shutting_down:\n                    logger.info(\"Browser closed during stream. Exiting cleanly.\")\n                    break\n                logger.error(f\"JS Extraction Error: {e}\")\n                consecutive_js_errors += 1\n                if consecutive_js_errors >= 30:\n                    logger.error(\"JS failed persistently for 30 consecutive attempts. Aborting.\")\n                    yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": \"[Error: Internal extraction logic failed persistently.]\"}\n                    break\n                await asyncio.sleep(0.15)\n                continue\n\n            current_text = state.get(\"text\", \"\")\n            is_running = state.get(\"is_running\", False)\n            is_done = state.get(\"is_done\", False)\n            new_turn_started = state.get(\"new_turn_started\", False)\n            has_error = state.get(\"has_error\", False)\n\n            # Check for fatal error banner in AI Studio\n            if has_error and not is_running and elapsed > 1.5:\n                logger.error(\"Turn ended with an error ('permission denied' / 'internal error') from Google AI Studio. Aborting without retry.\")\n                yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": \"[Error: Google AI Studio encountered an error ('permission denied' / 'internal error'). Please check chat or try again.]\"}\n                break\n\n            # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n            # 1. State: NO_RESPONSE_STARTED\n            # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n            if current_state == self.STATE_NO_RESPONSE_STARTED:\n                if is_running or new_turn_started or len(current_text) > 0:\n                    current_state = self.STATE_RESPONSE_IN_PROGRESS\n                    t_turn_detected = now\n                    t_last_growth = now\n                    logger.info(\n                        f\"[{case_count} cases] State -> RESPONSE_IN_PROGRESS at {t_turn_detected - t_submit:.2f}s \"\n                        f\"(is_running={is_running}, new_turn={new_turn_started}, initial_chars={len(current_text)})\"\n                    )\n                else:\n                    if elapsed > t_cfg[\"initial_start_timeout\"]:\n                        logger.error(f\"[{case_count} cases] Generation failed to start within {t_cfg['initial_start_timeout']:.0f}s. State: NO_RESPONSE_STARTED.\")\n                        yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": f\"[Error: NO_RESPONSE_STARTED - Google AI Studio did not start generating within {t_cfg['initial_start_timeout']:.0f}s]\"}\n                        break\n\n            # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n            # 2. State: RESPONSE_IN_PROGRESS\n            # ------------------------------------------------------------------\n            if current_state == self.STATE_RESPONSE_IN_PROGRESS:\n                # Milestone: First token/character detected\n                if len(current_text) > 0 and t_first_token is None:\n                    t_first_token = now\n                    logger.info(f\"[{case_count} cases] First token/character detected at {t_first_token - t_submit:.2f}s (len: {len(current_text)})\")\n\n                # Character growth detection\n                if len(current_text) > len(prev_text):\n                    delta = current_text[len(prev_text):]\n                    prev_text = current_text\n                    t_last_growth = now\n                    stability_start_time = None  # Reset stability timer when text actively grows\n                    yield {\"delta\": delta, \"text\": current_text}\n                else:\n                    # No character growth on this tick\n                    if len(current_text) == 0:\n                        # Model is still thinking / waiting to emit first token\n                        if (now - t_submit) > t_cfg[\"first_token_timeout\"]:\n                            if not is_running:\n                                logger.error(f\"[{case_count} cases] Model stopped without producing tokens after {now - t_submit:.1f}s.\")\n                                yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": f\"[Error: FIRST_TOKEN_TIMEOUT - Model finished without producing any text after {now - t_submit:.1f}s]\"}\n                            else:\n                                logger.error(f\"[{case_count} cases] Model thinking exceeded first_token_timeout ({t_cfg['first_token_timeout']:.0f}s).\")\n                                yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": f\"[Error: FIRST_TOKEN_TIMEOUT - Model stayed in thinking for >{t_cfg['first_token_timeout']:.0f}s without generating tokens]\"}\n                            break\n                    else:\n                        # Text has been emitted (len > 0), but did not grow on this tick\n                        if not is_running:\n                            # Generation has stopped running: check stability duration\n                            if stability_start_time is None:\n                                stability_start_time = now\n                            elif (now - stability_start_time) >= t_cfg[\"stability_duration\"]:\n                                # Stable for required duration!\n                                current_state = self.STATE_RESPONSE_COMPLETED\n                                logger.info(\n                                    f\"[{case_count} cases] State -> RESPONSE_COMPLETED via stability \"\n                                    f\"({t_cfg['stability_duration']:.1f}s stable at {len(current_text)} chars)\"\n                                )\n                                yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": current_text}\n                                break\n                        else:\n                            # is_running is True: NEVER timeout while running, EXCEPT stagnation guardrail\n                            stability_start_time = None\n                            if (now - t_last_growth) > t_cfg[\"stagnation_timeout\"]:\n                                logger.error(f\"[{case_count} cases] Stagnation: no character growth for {t_cfg['stagnation_timeout']:.0f}s while running.\")\n                                yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": f\"[Error: STAGNATION_TIMEOUT - Text generation stalled for {t_cfg['stagnation_timeout']:.0f}s]\"}\n                                break\n\n                    # Always yield the current state so non-streaming callers can access text\n                    yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": current_text}\n\n            await asyncio.sleep(0.1)\n        else:\n            # Loop ended due to hard_ceiling\n            if current_state != self.STATE_RESPONSE_COMPLETED:\n                logger.error(f\"[{case_count} cases] Hard ceiling reached ({t_cfg['hard_ceiling']:.0f}s). State: {current_state}. Aborting.\")\n                yield {\"delta\": \"\", \"text\": f\"[Error: HARD_CEILING_TIMEOUT - Request exceeded safe upper bound {t_cfg['hard_ceiling']:.0f}s]\"}\n\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n        # Detailed Timing Milestones Logging\n        # ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n        total_duration = time.time() - t_submit\n        turn_str = f\"{t_turn_detected - t_submit:.1f}s\" if t_turn_detected else \"N/A\"\n        first_token_str = f\"{t_first_token - t_submit:.1f}s\" if t_first_token else \"N/A\"\n        last_growth_str = f\"{t_last_growth - t_submit:.1f}s\" if (t_last_growth != t_submit) else \"N/A\"\n        completed_str = f\"{total_duration:.1f}s\" if current_state == self.STATE_RESPONSE_COMPLETED else \"INCOMPLETE\"\n\n        timing_summary = (\n            f\"{case_count} cases | \"\n            f\"first token: {first_token_str} | \"\n            f\"completed: {completed_str} | \"\n            f\"timeout: {t_cfg['first_token_timeout']:.0f}s\"\n        )\n        logger.info(f\"[TIMING] {timing_summary}\")\n        logger.info(\n            f\"[TIMING_DETAILS] {case_count} cases | state: {current_state} | \"\n            f\"turn detected: {turn_str} | first token: {first_token_str} | \"\n            f\"last growth: {last_growth_str} | completed: {completed_str} | \"\n            f\"total: {total_duration:.1f}s | chars: {len(prev_text)} | \"\n            f\"tier: {t_cfg['tier']}\"\n        )\n        print(f\"\\n[AI STUDIO TIMING] {timing_summary}\\n\")","StartLine":535,"TargetContent":"        # 7. Smart completion detection: stream response tokens until model message is complete\n        prev_text = \"\"\n        start_time = time.time()\n        generation_started = False\n        consecutive